# The lab's front door: one container on 443 terminating TLS for
# *.lab.twolfe.dev (the LAN path) and *.ts.twolfe.dev (the tailnet
# path — same names, reachable wherever Tailscale is), routing by
# hostname to containers on the shared `lab` network. Two ways in, one
# door — see tofu/records.tf for the decision.
#
# Routes do NOT live in this file. Each slice contributes a
# <slice>/caddy.caddyfile next to its compose file — a named host matcher
# plus a handle block — picked up by the import glob below from the repo
# mount. Adding a service never edits this slice (the same contract as
# flows/ and the job bridge). See README.md for the snippet shape.
#
# Certificates do NOT live here either: caddy is a pure proxy. The
# renew-certs job (flows/renew-certs/) obtains and renews ONE cert with
# both wildcard SANs via
# lego + DNS-01 and reloads caddy; this file just loads the result from
# the read-only /certs mount. One wildcard cert on purpose — per-name
# certs would list every internal hostname in public Certificate
# Transparency logs.

*.lab.twolfe.dev, *.ts.twolfe.dev {
	tls /certs/_.lab.twolfe.dev.crt /certs/_.lab.twolfe.dev.key

	import lab/*/caddy.caddyfile

	# Matcher-less handle matches anything the snippets didn't claim.
	# Must stay LAST: handle blocks run in order, first match wins.
	handle {
		respond "no such service" 404
	}
}
